# sftp — real-world examples

## Connect to a server on a non-standard port

```sh
# Be in the local directory where you want files to land first
sftp -oPort=60022 david@fileserver
```

## Connect to the homelab NAS with a specific key

```sh
sftp -i ~/.ssh/id_ed25519 david@mediaserver
```

## Pull a backup down from the homelab

```sh
sftp david@homelab
sftp> cd /srv/backups
sftp> lcd ~/restore
sftp> get site-backup-12.tar.gz
```

## Push a config up to a remote host

```sh
sftp> lcd ~/configs
sftp> cd /etc/nginx
sftp> put mediaserver.conf
```

## Common interactive commands

| Command | What it does              |
| ------- | ------------------------- |
| pwd     | remote working directory  |
| lpwd    | local working directory   |
| ls      | list remote directory     |
| lls     | list local directory      |
| cd      | change remote directory   |
| lcd     | change local directory    |
| get     | download remote → local   |
| put     | upload local → remote     |
| get -r  | recursive download        |
